      "textEn": "289\n\nThe so-called caste system of Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas and Shudras will be meaningless. As a result, whoever is powerful in any way,\nwill become the king or president, and in this way, the people will be so oppressed\nthat people will leave their homes and go to the forests (yasyanti girikananam), so that they can escape the oppression of those government officials\nwho are cruel and of looting-like nature. Therefore, the people should accept the Krishna consciousness movement\nor the Hare Krishna movement because it is the incarnation of God's word. Kali-Kale\nNaam-Rupre Krishna-Avatar—Now Krishna has appeared in the form of an incarnation of his own holy name. Therefore, when the people\nbecome absorbed in Krishna consciousness, only then can they hope for a good government, a good society, a complete life, and liberation from worldly bonds. Shri Raja said,\nThat, O King, by the conquest of the self-controlled.\nDone, by which clan, destroyed, by the Kshatriyas. 16. Meaning of the word.\n\nShri-Raja said—Maharaj Parikshit asked—What? That—That crime; Bhagavatam—Towards God; Rajanyah—Of the king; Kritam—Done; Yena—By which; Kulam—Clan; Nashtam—Destroyed; Kshatriyanam—Of the Kshatriya dynasty; Abhikshnashah—Again and again I.\n\nKing Parikshit asked Shukdev Goswami: What was the crime of those kings, because of which the incarnation of God, Parashurama, destroyed the Kshatriya dynasty\nAgain and again? Shreebadarayaniruvacha\nHaihayanamadhipatirarjunah Kshatriyarshabhah. Dattam Narayanamshamshamaradhya parikarmabhih. 17). From the sky, one hundred thousand are difficult to obtain. Abyahateendriyaaujah shritejoviryashobalam. 18. Yogeshwaratvam aiswaryam gunayatraanimadayah.\nLike the wind in the speed of a chariot. 19. Meaning of the word.\n\nShri-Badarayanih said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami answered—The king of Haihayas—The king of Haihayas; Arjuna—Kartavirya Arjuna;\nKshatriya-Rishabha—The best among the Kshatriyas; Dattam—To Dattatreya; N